From 79478dab269e0c12e3c1f4c97b46f961389da8a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jempa <jempamartensson@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:50:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 36/39] ACEScg color space; image "colorspace" override; film
 keeps its color space in PFMs (for hdPbrt)

- RGBColorSpace::ACEScg ("acescg": AP1 primaries, ACES white, its own
  RGB-to-spectrum table from rgb2spec_opt, which learns the ACEScg gamut),
  also found by Lookup from EXR chromaticities.
- imagemap textures, diffuse area lights and infinite lights take
  "string colorspace": the image's RGB primaries, overriding the file's
  metadata (which defaults to sRGB primaries).
- RGBFilm "bool hdpbrtkeepcolorspace": a PFM is written in the film's color
  space (Image::Write converts formats without color metadata to sRGB; the
  display stream never did).
